# Ur/Web Portability Notes

This document describes portability requirements and environment overrides for
building Ur/Web on POSIX-compliant systems.

## POSIX Baseline

The build system targets POSIX.1-2008. Shell scripts use `#!/bin/sh` and avoid
bash-specific features.

## Required Tools

- **sh** — POSIX shell
- **cc** — C compiler (C11)
- **make** — GNU Make (for BearSSL; build uses ninja/samurai)
- **MLton** — Standard ML compiler
- **mllex** — ML lexer generator (MLton bundle or SML/NJ ml-lex)
- **mlyacc** — ML parser generator (MLton bundle or SML/NJ ml-yacc)
- **sed**, **awk** — POSIX utilities
- **pkg-config** — Optional; used to discover ICU when available

## Optional Tools

- **pkg-config** — If absent, set `ICU_CFLAGS` and `ICU_LIBS` (or `ICU_INCLUDES`
  and `ICU_LIBS`) manually, or configure will probe common paths
- **samu** / **ninja** — Build driver (ninja-compatible)
- **lsof** — Used by tests to free ports; when absent, tests may fail if ports
  are in use from a previous run

## Environment Overrides

| Variable        | Purpose                                      |
|-----------------|----------------------------------------------|
| CC              | C compiler (default: cc)                     |
| MLTON           | MLton executable (default: mlton)            |
| MLLEX           | Lexer generator (default: mllex)             |
| MLYACC          | Parser generator (default: mlyacc)           |
| ICU_CFLAGS      | ICU include flags (when pkg-config absent)   |
| ICU_INCLUDES    | Same as ICU_CFLAGS                           |
| ICU_LIBS        | ICU link flags                               |
| PKG_CONFIG_PATH | Help pkg-config find ICU                     |
| DESTDIR         | Staging prefix for install                   |
| TMPDIR          | Temp directory (default: /tmp)               |

Example without pkg-config:

```sh
ICU_CFLAGS="-I/usr/include" ICU_LIBS="-licui18n -licuuc" ./configure
```

Example with SML/NJ tools:

```sh
MLLEX=ml-lex MLYACC=ml-yacc ./configure
```

## Supported Platforms

- **Linux** — _GNU_SOURCE defined when needed
- **macOS** — _DARWIN_C_SOURCE defined when needed
- **BSD** — No extra macros; standard C11
- **Solaris / Illumos** — __EXTENSIONS__ when needed

## Test Dependencies

Running `samu test` requires:

- **sqlite3** — Database for demo and driver tests
- **curl** — HTTP requests
- **node**, **npm** — Playwright tests
- **jq** — Optional; improves endpoints test output
- **lsof** — Optional; frees ports before tests
- **nc** — Optional; fallback for port readiness (curl used when nc absent)
